-- What stays legal beside a mixfix rule: clauses written with a name of their
-- own first, whether the name is a new one or a constructor's; a second
-- definition of the same words with a GIVEN of its own, for other types; and
-- the rule itself, written with a word between its inputs and no clauses at
-- all. The not-ok/tc/pattern-matching-mixfix-form-* files are what is refused.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
c `costs` n MEANS n

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      s IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
c `costs` s MEANS 7

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE price Red 0 IS 1
DECIDE price c n IS n

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE Green 0 IS 7
DECIDE Green n IS n

#EVAL Red `costs` 0
#EVAL Red `costs` "x"
#EVAL price Red 0
#EVAL price Blue 4
